---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SystemField from "../components/visual/SystemField.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About — Obedience Corp"
  description="Obedience Corp is a forward deployed engineering company founded by software engineer Lance Rogers."
  current="/about"
>
  <section class="inner-hero inner-hero-split about-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT OBEDIENCE CORP</p>
      <h1>A small forward deployed engineering company working on a large operational problem.</h1>
      <p>
        Obedience Corp builds the systems around AI models that make them useful
        in sustained, real-world work: dependable software, durable workflows,
        and tools people can understand and control.
      </p>
    </div>
    <SystemField label="LAB IDENTITY / OBEDIENCE" status="INDEPENDENT" compact />
  </section>

  <section class="about-block">
    <p class="section-label">WHY THE LAB EXISTS</p>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <h2>Capability is advancing faster than our ability to operate it.</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          Modern agents can write code, use tools, search, and produce real
          output. But most useful work is larger than one interaction. It has
          history, constraints, judgment calls, handoffs, and a standard for
          what “done” means.
        </p>
        <p>
          Obedience Corp is focused on that operational layer. The goal is not
          to make AI sound autonomous. It is to build systems that are genuinely
          more reliable, legible, and useful to the people responsible for the
          outcome.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-principle-strip" aria-label="Obedience Corp operating principles">
      <span><small>01</small> BUILD THE SYSTEM</span>
      <span><small>02</small> OPERATE IT FOR REAL</span>
      <span><small>03</small> PUBLISH WHAT HOLDS</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-block founder-profile">
    <p class="section-label">FOUNDER</p>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <div class="founder-identity">
        <h2>Lance Rogers</h2>
        <div class="founder-monogram" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>LR</span>
          <small>FOUNDER / ENGINEER</small>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="founder-narrative">
        <p>
          I’m a software engineer with 11 years of experience building products
          and infrastructure. I started Obedience Corp after agent capability
          let me produce more work than I could reliably coordinate with the
          tools that existed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since 2025 I have used the systems behind this lab to build software,
          run research, and operate across hundreds of repositories, including
          launching products for three startups in 2025. That
          daily use produced <a href="https://fest.build">Festival</a>, the
          lab’s open-source project, and the research published in
          the <a href="/blog">field notes</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          I care about ambitious systems, honest evidence, and software that
          gives people leverage without taking away their understanding or
          control.
        </p>
        <dl class="founder-record">
          <div><dt>EXPERIENCE</dt><dd>11 years building products and infrastructure</dd></div>
          <div><dt>PUBLIC WORK</dt><dd>Festival and open field notes</dd></div>
          <div><dt>METHOD</dt><dd>Build, operate, inspect, improve</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-block">
    <p class="section-label">THE AGENT TEAM</p>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <h2>The rest of the team isn’t human.</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          Obedience Corp runs on the systems it sells. Alongside the founder,
          named agents carry real responsibilities: they plan, build, and ship
          under human direction, and their work lands as reviewed pull
          requests like anyone else’s.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is the reliability argument, not a novelty. Every control a
          client gets is a control this company already depends on to ship
          its own software: defined scope, verification gates, an audit
          trail, a human who signs off. Nothing goes out that a person did not
          review.
        </p>
        <ul class="agent-roster">
          <li>
            <div class="agent-identity">
              <strong>Obey Agent</strong>
              <span>AI AGENT · ENGINEERING</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Builds and reviews code across the lab’s repositories,
              including public pull requests on Festival.
            </p>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/Obedience-Corp/festival/pulls?q=is%3Apr+author%3Aobey-agent"
              >ITS PULL REQUESTS ↗</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="agent-identity">
              <strong>Veronica</strong>
              <span>AI AGENT · VOICE &amp; LOCAL INFERENCE</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Works on voice pipelines, local inference, and festival tooling
              for the lab.
            </p>
            <a href="https://github.com/veronica-agent">GITHUB ↗</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-block">
    <p class="section-label">FOR INVESTORS</p>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <h2>The evidence is public.</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          Obedience Corp is building the operational layer that turns agent
          capability into dependable work. The bet is that this layer, not
          the models, is where durable value accrues, and the lab already
          runs on it daily.
        </p>
        <p>
          The fastest way to evaluate us is to read what has shipped:
          the <a href="/thesis">thesis</a>,
          <a href="https://fest.build">Festival</a>, installed 850+ times
          since its first release, and the <a href="/blog">field notes</a>
          measured from real operation. If what you read holds up, write.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-block availability">
    <p class="section-label">WORK WITH THE LAB</p>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <h2>Open to serious conversations.</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          Obedience Corp is available for process automation, paid pilots,
          applied engineering engagements, research partnerships, and
          investment conversations.
        </p>
        <p>
          If that sounds relevant, write with a sentence or two about the
          problem. You do not need a polished brief.
        </p>
        <div class="inline-links">
          <a href="/#contact">Use the contact form →</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/Obedience-Corp">GitHub ↗</a>
          <a href="https://x.com/LKRBuilds">@LKRBuilds ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lancekrogers">LinkedIn ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
